<!-- noupdate="0" DELIBERATELY (W13) — see pb_home_hub/data/pb_sidebar.xml. -->
<odoo noupdate="0">

    <!-- OPERATE › People.

         It absorbs Employees and Contracts (its first two lenses) and the whole
         PLANNING section (its third, which is a LAUNCHER over those seven
         screens unchanged — owner ruling). Every one of those nine rail records
         survives, retired into the 900 band, and every one of their actions
         still works, so this item claims their tags and xmlids: the two
         cockpits' tags plus the two DETAIL cockpits nothing on the rail ever
         claimed (`pb_employee_detail`, `pb_contract_detail` — opening an
         employee from anywhere used to leave the rail blank), the Planning
         dashboard's client-action TAG, and the six planning act_window xmlids.

         `hr.employee` and `hr.contract` are claimed here and nowhere else. That
         is the second of the two double-claims Cycle 1 found and pinned rather
         than fixed: `item_employees` and `item_contracts` both claimed
         `hr.contract`, and the rail's active-item index is FLAT and
         last-writer-wins (W71), so Contracts won by ordering accident.

         GATED SINCE ACCESS P4, in TWO LANES read as an OR — see
         `pb_payhub/data/pb_sidebar.xml` for why the lane written here is a
         PERMISSION and the other lane (the roles) is written by
         `pb_vendor_access` onto the row.

         `hr.group_hr_user` and not the pb_hr_payroll_base tiers the two retired
         items carried: this entry is about `hr.employee` and `hr.contract`, and
         the group whose ACL actually opens those records is the HR one. It is
         also implied by every tier above it, so a manager keeps the door.

         `(4, ref(…))` never `(6, 0, …)` — an ADD, so `pb_demo`'s join survives
         the next upgrade of this module.

         The shell still gates its lenses from the ACL of the model behind each
         one (W95), which stays the narrower and more honest answer about what
         somebody can do once they are inside. -->
    <record id="item_people" model="pb.sidebar.item">
        <field name="section_id" ref="pb_sidebar.sec_payrun"/>
        <field name="groups_id" eval="[(4, ref('hr.group_hr_user'))]"/>
        <field name="name">People</field>
        <field name="icon">users</field>
        <field name="sequence">20</field>
        <field name="action_xmlid">pb_people_hub.action_pb_people_hub</field>
        <field name="action_tag">pb_people_hub</field>
        <field name="match_action_tags">pb_people_hub,pb_people,pb_contracts,pb_employee_detail,pb_contract_detail,wfp_dashboard</field>
        <field name="match_action_xmlids">pb_hr_workforce_planning.action_wfp_scenario,pb_hr_workforce_planning.action_wfp_forecast,pb_hr_workforce_planning.action_wfp_grade,pb_hr_workforce_planning.action_wfp_merit_matrix,pb_hr_workforce_planning.action_wfp_cycle,pb_hr_workforce_planning.action_wfp_tagging_wizard</field>
        <field name="match_models">hr.employee,hr.contract</field>
    </record>

</odoo>
